          "title": "You'll want to know: зубрить",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "зубрить (zubrít) — \"to cram, to learn by rote\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Перед экзаменом он зубрил всю ночь. Péred ekzámenom on zubríl vsyu noch. Before the exam he crammed all night."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; present зубрю, зубришь; perfective вызубрить. Colloquial."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "зубрить (zubrít) is usually linked with зуб \"a tooth\", inherited from Proto-Slavic zǫbŭ: to gnaw away at a subject until it is learned."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
